# mobile(gui-plugins-v2-2-7, issue #194 of the registry / GitHub issue #194): the GUI-plugins mobile
# faces re-derived on the v2.2.7 surface — the narrow-screen entries the v2.2.7 pin absorbed away
# with the goal/sources/btw reworks, re-landed as the pin-native faces demand. Four retired payloads
# fold into this one patch (their old .patch files stay untouched on disk for audit):
#   D1  (M-038, session-btw-narrow-entry row): the /btw command gate drops the desktop-width term
#       (enabled: mounted(); desktop width is unchanged by construction — at >=768px !layout.narrow()
#       is constant, so the old gate already reduced to mounted()) and the BuiltinPanel gains the
#       narrow-screen mobile face (order 80, kind menu, icon comment — the More-drawer entry after
#       sources 60, the pin-native faces being review 10 / file 20 / terminal 30 / context 40 /
#       details 50; goal's old order 70 is gone because v2.2.7 goal is the native ComposerPill, not
#       a panel — no face is renumbered).
#   D2/D3  (M-038 + the 10th target): the mobile render path dispatches on the panel id ("main";
#       chat ids are UUIDs, so the dispatch cannot collide) and shows the most recent stored chat
#       once the session's store is ready (an empty container before that, the tabs'
#       hidden-until-ready semantics), else the honest mobile.none empty state. v2.2.7's createBtw
#       exports ask/tab/view/retry/remove but not the saved list the old D3 read (chats.at(-1)), so
#       btw/model.ts gains the minimal `saved` accessor export (same reader the tab/view accessors
#       dispatch through) — the 10th target of this patch. The mobile view has no tab-close channel,
#       so chats asked on narrow screens reappear as desktop strip tabs when the viewport widens
#       (the close path lives there); the store keeps the upstream "kept until its tab closes"
#       semantics. btw/panel.tsx and btw/index.ts stay pin-verbatim (probe-locked sha1).
#   S1  (M-036 sources half, session-goal-sources-panels row): the sources side panel re-lands its
#       narrow-screen face — mobile face order 60 (kind menu, icon globe), the gate-off honest
#       panel.disabled empty state (the fallback is only reachable from the always-present More
#       drawer entry), the panel-id "turn" dispatch rendering the most recent turn with sources,
#       the panel.none empty state, and the panel.title/panel.disabled/panel.none i18n keys.
#   S2  (M-036 settings half, session-goal-sources-panels row): the Settings -> Experimental Sources
#       gate row re-lands on the v2.2.7 page (SettingsRow + data-action="settings-sources" Switch,
#       en/zh row.sources.* keys per the #193 pairing convention). The old storedToggle/
#       setStoredToggle write path does not exist at v2.2.7 — the row flips the knob DECLARED ONCE by
#       session-ui's sources experiment through the new setSourcesEnabled accessor (the knob instance
#       captured once in that module; re-registering motionTuning.toggle("sources.enabled") anywhere
#       would Map.set-clobber the instance and leave the row showing on while the experiment stays
#       off; motionTuning.set persists and notifies, so the debug Knobs panel and the
#       sourcesExperiment store stay in sync via subscribe).
#   F6  (extensions-flyout-webview row): the details flyout open-state rule
#       `.session-service-flyout[data-open] &` flattens to the non-nested ancestor-selector form
#       (WebView 114 ?inline CSS injection cannot parse this nesting; the &:dir(rtl) and
#       [data-motion] nesting stay nested — a progressive loss on old WebViews, recorded). The
#       v2.2.7 rule carries no transition block (the old patch's transition lines are pin-absorbed
#       upstream), so the flatten is the 3-property open-state rule only.
# Everything else the four payloads carried is pin-absorbed native at v2.2.7 (the goal data layer
# and schema/goal.ts, the session-ui sources subsystem incl. the graduated sources-expand-machine,
# the timeline turnSources hooks, the motion spring/loop modules, outline-steer, ui.sources.* i18n,
# the SourcesProvider host wrapper): carried by NO hunk here. Marker:
